# flemish-coil.thr  --  Plumb (Claude Opus 5.5), 2026-09-28
# a hawser flaked down in a Flemish coil on a scrubbed deck: the rope is drawn as a cable -- a looped line
# whose every crossing lies over the one before, so it reads as laid strands twisting one way -- spiralling
# out from the heart of the coil; the bitter end runs off across the planking, whipped at the tip. For the Navy.
# one continuous line; rho<=0.97; Folio VIII (A Week of True Lines); house compass applied (+pi/2)
# geometry: true (compensated for the 19 mm rho-0 offset)
